From 5820ad4f2ed8930397f2b37e0cf1c1c54cdb54d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 15:31:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno: A22X per-draw DEALLOC bisect (Gemini round 5)

Round-4 falsified end-of-tile-loop DEALLOC: emitting VS_DEALLOC
(0x00) + PS_DEALLOC (0x01) AFTER all per-tile work has no effect
on the 0x0ee2 cycle-counter advance rate.

Gemini round-5 hypothesis: the slot allocator is bound tightly to
each draw and needs immediate deallocation after the draw, not
deferred to end of submit.

This emits the deallocation pair after EVERY CP_DRAW_INDX (in the
shared fd_draw() helper, gated on is_a22x screen + env var).
Per-render flow (Mesa A22X):
  1. binning CP_DRAW_INDX
  2. -> emit VS_DEALLOC + PS_DEALLOC (NEW)
  3. user CP_DRAW_INDX
  4. -> emit VS_DEALLOC + PS_DEALLOC (NEW)
  5. resolve RECTLIST CP_DRAW_INDX
  6. -> emit VS_DEALLOC + PS_DEALLOC (NEW)
  N. ... per tile

Default (no FD2_PER_DRAW_DEALLOC env) = byte-identical to prior.

Test: FD2_PER_DRAW_DEALLOC=1 FD2_FLUSH_MULTIPLIER=1 cap-binary
Read 0x0ee2 via debugfs.  Expected outcomes:
  a) Cycle PINS at boot value (0x15000002): per-draw deallocation
     model confirmed.  Make unconditional in follow-up.
  b) Cycle unchanged: the slot tracking is independent of draw
     proximity too.  Confirms architectural difference between
     Mesa and vendor cmdstreams.
  c) Hang: per-draw event emission unsafe in this position.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_draw.h | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_draw.h b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_draw.h
index 3f2bcba1560..fc2295e9d65 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_draw.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_draw.h
@@ -103,6 +103,24 @@ fd_draw(struct fd_batch *batch, struct fd_ringbuffer *ring,
 
    emit_marker(ring, 7);
 
+   /* A22X per-draw DEALLOC bisect (FD2_PER_DRAW_DEALLOC=1).
+    *
+    * Round-4 falsified end-of-tile-loop DEALLOC events as
+    * cycle-fixers.  Gemini round-5 hypothesis: events need to be
+    * emitted RIGHT AFTER each CP_DRAW_INDX, not deferred to end of
+    * batch.  Tests whether slot deallocation is tied to draw
+    * proximity.
+    *
+    * Emits VS_DEALLOC (0x00) + PS_DEALLOC (0x01) after every draw.
+    * Gated on is_a22x screen.
+    */
+   if (is_a22x(batch->ctx->screen) && getenv("FD2_PER_DRAW_DEALLOC")) {
+      OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_EVENT_WRITE, 1);
+      OUT_RING(ring, 0x00);  /* VS_DEALLOC */
+      OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_EVENT_WRITE, 1);
+      OUT_RING(ring, 0x01);  /* PS_DEALLOC */
+   }
+
    fd_reset_wfi(batch);
 }
 
